WEBVTT

00:00:28.778 --> 00:00:30.071
Hey, is it here?

00:00:30.071 --> 00:00:33.491
We can't do it. Call Nina Antalk!

00:00:36.077 --> 00:00:38.079
C'mon, cut the crap!

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:42.500
What's goin' on? Hey, Zuellni!

00:00:51.926 --> 00:00:55.055
<i>Brave your truth and brave yourself</i>

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:58.600
<i>So we can go somewhere with the dite</i>

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:06.024
<i>Keep hope alive, now we</i>
<i>wanna find the new world</i>

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:11.780
<i>Chizu o ushinatte samayotteiru machi</i>

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.241
<i>Owariyuku sekai demo</i>

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:21.956
<i>Karada no oku de hashiru</i>
<i>no o yamenai inochi o kikasete</i>

00:01:21.956 --> 00:01:25.251
<i>Tayasanai hikari o tozasanai hitomi ni</i>

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:28.630
<i>Kawaitemo yakitsuketa</i>

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:35.220
<i>Kizutsuku koto mo naku</i>
<i>te ni suru mono nante nanimo shinjinai</i>

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:41.142
<i>Dareka ni mukatta hitosuji no omoi wa</i>

00:01:41.142 --> 00:01:49.025
<i>Yoake no you ni hagane no yami o kirisaku</i>

00:01:49.025 --> 00:01:53.363
<i>Itsuka brave your truth and brave yourself</i>

00:01:53.363 --> 00:01:57.033
<i>Dakara tsuyoku kaeru</i>

00:01:57.033 --> 00:02:02.997
<i>Kasaneta chikara mo inori mo</i>

00:02:02.997 --> 00:02:06.668
<i>Kousa suru mirai, kakaeta negai</i>

00:02:06.668 --> 00:02:10.088
<i>Dare no te ni mo watasenai</i>

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:11.631
<i>Just tough and alive</i>

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:16.636
<i>Kokoro o tsuraneru</i>

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:31.568
<i>In any case...</i>

00:02:31.568 --> 00:02:33.611
<i>As Kanalis says, I suppose</i>
<i>we cannot keep the seat</i>

00:02:34.863 --> 00:02:37.574
<i>of the last Heaven's Blade empty forever.</i>

00:02:38.575 --> 00:02:40.201
<i>Also...</i>

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.537
Savalis?

00:02:42.537 --> 00:02:46.666
I hope all has been well with you, my queen...

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.460
though it would appear not.

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:51.796
Could this be because of the Fallen One?

00:02:53.214 --> 00:02:57.010
I beg you let me be of
service to you, Your Majesty.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.345
You wish to go?

00:02:58.345 --> 00:03:00.096
I have great interest in doing so.

00:03:00.096 --> 00:03:01.639
You want it.

00:03:01.639 --> 00:03:03.266
I do want it.

00:03:03.266 --> 00:03:08.104
I would like to use that power,
which equals Your Majesty's.

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:12.400
Well, I shall consider it.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:13.693
Where are you going?

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.695
I have an important task.

00:03:19.824 --> 00:03:23.328
"Zuellni Run Amok
and the Contaminoid Offensive!"

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:37.550
Whatcha doin'?

00:03:40.387 --> 00:03:42.514
What are <i>you </i>doing, Senior?

00:03:42.514 --> 00:03:45.767
I've been like this for quite some time.

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:48.228
I think I'm about to be quite embarrassed...

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:50.271
Then hurry up and get down!

00:03:50.271 --> 00:03:51.606
Ah, how cruel!

00:03:51.606 --> 00:03:53.817
Hey, wait!

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:04.744
Look, don't be so mad. I'll take you out to eat.

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:10.125
No thank you. You always take
me to some expensive-looking place...

00:04:10.125 --> 00:04:12.419
And I fear a physical danger!

00:04:12.419 --> 00:04:16.631
Physical danger? Well who knows...

00:04:16.631 --> 00:04:19.009
Just please stop that!

00:04:19.009 --> 00:04:25.140
I <i>can't </i>stop it. I couldn't very
well rob myself of this pleasure!

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:27.767
I don't care about your
"pleasures," Shinora-<i>san</i>!

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:32.355
Now, now. You intend to leave Glendan, yes?

00:04:33.565 --> 00:04:36.443
Well, if the person you're
waiting for won't come back,

00:04:36.443 --> 00:04:40.864
then you go after him.
It's not as if I don't understand.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:50.957
But only a city's electronic spirit knows
where that Regios will go.

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:53.668
Even if you're lucky enough to find the city,

00:04:53.668 --> 00:04:57.547
what if you're attacked by contaminoids
on the way or something?

00:04:57.547 --> 00:05:01.676
There's no reason for you to
put yourself in such danger, is there?

00:05:01.676 --> 00:05:05.347
Uh... What's his name,
your childhood boyfriend?

00:05:05.347 --> 00:05:06.473
Layfon.

00:05:06.473 --> 00:05:12.645
Oh, that's right! I don't
think Layfon-<i>kun </i>would want that.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:16.608
But while I stay here, Layfon is...

00:05:16.608 --> 00:05:20.153
I know! Right now, what I most need to do

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:23.114
is study to protect the orphanage.

00:05:23.114 --> 00:05:27.911
I can't use the money that Layfon
left me to pay for travel.

00:05:27.911 --> 00:05:28.828
In that case...

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:31.706
But! That just makes me think...

00:05:31.706 --> 00:05:35.377
Should I let Layfon suffer like this, alone?

00:05:35.377 --> 00:05:37.170
--Isn't there something else that I can be doing?

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.422
<i>--I wonder if this was counter-productive...</i>
--Isn't there something else that I can be doing?

00:05:39.422 --> 00:05:42.759
And there's no response to my letters.

00:05:42.759 --> 00:05:47.263
He couldn't be sick or injured
right now, could he?

00:05:47.263 --> 00:05:48.807
No, no. Of course not!

00:05:48.807 --> 00:05:51.267
There's no way <i>he </i>could get injured!

00:05:52.102 --> 00:05:53.353
How do you know that?

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:55.063
Uh, that is...

00:05:55.063 --> 00:05:57.190
I'm just saying, don't worry.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:00.193
Not hearing from him is proof he's all right.

00:06:01.695 --> 00:06:03.321
Layfon...

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:07.534
Are you an idiot?

00:06:07.534 --> 00:06:09.119
What, out of the blue?

00:06:09.119 --> 00:06:11.287
You make me want to say it.

00:06:11.287 --> 00:06:15.291
If you'd lost even a little more blood,
you would have died.

00:06:15.291 --> 00:06:19.671
I'm sorry. But I never thought
that would happen to me...

00:06:19.671 --> 00:06:22.757
And? How are your wounds?

00:06:22.757 --> 00:06:25.385
It looks like the biggest problem is my spine.

00:06:25.385 --> 00:06:30.181
They need to operate to remove a
fragment of spine from my spinal cord.

00:06:30.181 --> 00:06:32.892
Then the next competition will
be impossible for you.

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:36.646
Yes. But it looks like
Nina isn't going to forfeit.

00:06:37.731 --> 00:06:42.527
Because this next one is the big match,
against Vanzeh's 1st Platoon.

00:06:42.527 --> 00:06:44.446
She got even more fired up, saying she could

00:06:44.446 --> 00:06:46.573
pull it off without me.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.950
She came here?

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:51.077
Yes, this morning.

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:53.830
She missed her classes just for that?

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:57.042
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:06:57.042 --> 00:06:59.669
Now that you mention it, I guess so.

00:06:59.669 --> 00:07:02.422
The two of you are quite <i>close</i>, I see!

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:07.552
Don't you think that's cruel? I'm injured...

00:07:07.552 --> 00:07:10.638
The job of the sick is to hurry and get well.

00:07:10.638 --> 00:07:13.266
By all means, feel better!

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:24.903
Still, talk about unlucky, huh?

00:07:24.903 --> 00:07:29.699
Layfon's surgery being on
the same day as the competition...

00:07:29.699 --> 00:07:33.912
Enough of that.
Even if Layfon got released early,

00:07:33.912 --> 00:07:35.914
we couldn't force him to exert himself.

00:07:35.914 --> 00:07:40.126
But isn't going on without
him being too reckless?

00:07:40.126 --> 00:07:44.130
Don't worry.
There are many different ways to fight.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:46.132
I hope so...

00:07:48.176 --> 00:07:50.387
<i>When it happened...</i>

00:07:52.639 --> 00:07:55.725
Hey! Where are you? Layfon!

00:07:55.725 --> 00:07:57.936
Answer us! Layfon!

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:06.027
<i>What was I thinking of?</i>

00:08:17.455 --> 00:08:19.374
<i>Then next competition.</i>

00:08:19.374 --> 00:08:24.796
<i>The idea of going without Layfon</i>
<i>made me feel anxious, hopeless, resigned.</i>

00:08:24.796 --> 00:08:27.007
<i>I felt like it was all over.</i>

00:08:30.969 --> 00:08:33.096
Pitiful.

00:08:33.096 --> 00:08:35.056
I've gotten stronger, too!

00:08:35.056 --> 00:08:38.351
I can't just keep relying
on Layfon for everything!

00:08:49.738 --> 00:08:51.072
Sharnid...

00:08:51.072 --> 00:08:52.532
Hey.

00:08:54.492 --> 00:08:57.120
How's Dinn? Is he well?

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:00.665
If you cared, you could go see for yourself.

00:09:00.665 --> 00:09:05.045
I don't think he'll forgive me,
so I'm gonna hold off on that.

00:09:05.045 --> 00:09:07.881
Then what? Do you wish something of me?

00:09:07.881 --> 00:09:13.720
Yeah. You've heard rumors, right?
Our ace member's been badly injured.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:16.931
You're not actually going
to ask me to take his place, are you?

00:09:16.931 --> 00:09:20.268
As a full-fledged member, if you like.

00:09:20.268 --> 00:09:24.314
I refuse. There is no
way I could fight alongside you!

00:09:24.314 --> 00:09:27.400
The bonds the three of us shared are gone.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.693
Quite right.

00:09:28.693 --> 00:09:34.240
But I didn't ask you because
I wanted to do things like the old days.

00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:37.327
Without Dinn, there's no way that we could.

00:09:37.327 --> 00:09:42.832
What we need right now is <i>you</i>, Dalsiena Matelna.

00:09:42.832 --> 00:09:46.795
We're not after a replacement for Layfon.

00:09:46.795 --> 00:09:48.630
Also, Siena...

00:09:48.963 --> 00:09:52.175
The bonds the three of us had are broken.

00:09:54.135 --> 00:09:56.888
But the promise we made that day...

00:09:59.474 --> 00:10:01.810
I haven't given up on it.

00:10:04.688 --> 00:10:09.526
Neither have you.
And unless I miss my guess...

00:10:20.704 --> 00:10:22.330
Dinn.

00:10:25.709 --> 00:10:27.585
Huh?! Lay-ton!

00:10:27.585 --> 00:10:30.505
Oh. Naruki, Mifi!

00:10:30.505 --> 00:10:33.091
You're up and about?!

00:10:33.091 --> 00:10:36.094
Yeah. I can handle this much.

00:10:38.179 --> 00:10:40.265
Huh? Dalsiena-<i>san</i>?

00:10:40.265 --> 00:10:43.977
Yup! She's making her dynamic
entry into the 17th Platoon!

00:10:43.977 --> 00:10:45.812
It's kind of a scoop, huh?

00:10:45.812 --> 00:10:48.690
I thought I should tell you lickety-split!

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:54.112
Oh. Dalsiena-<i>san </i>can definitely
hold her own. I'm relieved to hear that.

00:10:54.112 --> 00:10:56.448
That's sort of a
depressed-looking face, though...

00:10:56.448 --> 00:10:59.284
Huh? No, not at all.

00:10:59.284 --> 00:11:04.414
It's just, realizing it'll work
out without me makes me a little...

00:11:05.665 --> 00:11:07.375
What are you getting down about?

00:11:07.375 --> 00:11:09.878
Of course it'd be better if you were there!

00:11:09.878 --> 00:11:15.175
Yes, that's right. But the 17th isn't
hoping things will work,

00:11:15.175 --> 00:11:17.260
they're doing their best to <i>make </i>it work.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:18.678
Yeah, right?

00:11:18.678 --> 00:11:22.640
Oh... Is that so?

00:11:23.433 --> 00:11:27.062
By the way, um... Where's Mayshen?

00:11:27.979 --> 00:11:32.442
What's wrong with Mayshen?
Her being her, is she maybe...?

00:11:32.442 --> 00:11:38.865
Well, she's convinced
it's her fault you got hurt.

00:11:42.702 --> 00:11:43.745
I thought so.

00:11:43.745 --> 00:11:49.167
Ah, but don't worry!
We'll do something about her.

00:11:49.167 --> 00:11:53.546
Lay-ton, the main thing on
your mind should be getting well.

00:11:53.546 --> 00:11:55.757
Yeah. Thank you.

00:11:58.051 --> 00:11:59.678
You're...

00:12:01.262 --> 00:12:04.057
I've been waiting for you.

00:12:05.308 --> 00:12:10.980
Actually, the president wishes
to have a word with you in private.

00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:13.817
Again?

00:12:29.124 --> 00:12:31.126
What the?!

00:12:35.338 --> 00:12:37.465
I'll fucking kill ya!

00:12:38.466 --> 00:12:43.054
You can still talk. But you know what?
You can't beat me.

00:12:43.054 --> 00:12:46.057
I guess not, if I'm by myself.

00:12:55.066 --> 00:12:56.943
Hey, don't go in there!

00:12:56.943 --> 00:13:00.113
We're on the job. Give us the details.

00:13:00.113 --> 00:13:01.573
Yes, sir.

00:13:01.573 --> 00:13:05.618
The Aurora Particle ratio
in this area went extremely high.

00:13:05.618 --> 00:13:07.454
Any other problems 'round here?

00:13:07.454 --> 00:13:09.748
Nothing's been reported at this point.

00:13:09.748 --> 00:13:12.334
We want to interview the eyewitnesses.

00:13:12.334 --> 00:13:16.004
They've all been transported,
but they're not in good shape at all.

00:13:16.004 --> 00:13:19.090
It'll be a while before
they'll be up and around.

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:20.717
I see.

00:13:27.182 --> 00:13:29.768
The competition will soon begin.

00:13:29.768 --> 00:13:34.314
In the end, will it be Vanzeh's
1st Platoon that comes out on top?

00:13:35.523 --> 00:13:36.941
That's how we'll play this.

00:13:36.941 --> 00:13:37.901
Sir!

00:13:37.901 --> 00:13:40.862
Or will it be the 17th Platoon,
with Dalsiena-che-Matelna

00:13:40.862 --> 00:13:43.865
as the injured Layfon's
last-minute replacement?

00:13:43.865 --> 00:13:47.660
Their teamwork will be something to watch!

00:13:59.798 --> 00:14:01.257
What's our plan?

00:14:01.257 --> 00:14:05.011
I'll go ahead on their right flank,
get their attention.

00:14:05.011 --> 00:14:09.265
Dalsiena, you back up Sharnid
and Felli and attack their left flank

00:14:09.265 --> 00:14:11.476
and open up a route to their sniping point.

00:14:11.476 --> 00:14:15.563
This time, we're going to be the aggressors.
If you fail, we lose.

00:14:15.563 --> 00:14:16.731
You're all right with that?

00:14:16.731 --> 00:14:19.818
I ask that you don't worry about me.

00:14:21.027 --> 00:14:23.071
Okay, let's do it.

00:14:23.071 --> 00:14:25.281
All right. We will win!

00:14:29.285 --> 00:14:33.790
It's been a while since we've seen her:
Dalsiena-che-Matelna!

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:35.417
Dalsiena!

00:15:07.574 --> 00:15:09.993
All right, come get me!

00:15:12.328 --> 00:15:14.205
Two enemies, moving out on your right flank.

00:15:14.205 --> 00:15:15.999
The rest are all headed this way.

00:15:15.999 --> 00:15:17.042
What?

00:15:17.042 --> 00:15:18.793
Shoot! They saw through it?

00:15:18.793 --> 00:15:20.086
Hey, Siena!

00:15:20.086 --> 00:15:22.505
It's all right. Leave it to me.

00:15:31.806 --> 00:15:35.310
I'm sorry... about before.

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:38.063
I'm not worried about it. It was an accident.

00:15:38.063 --> 00:15:40.690
You didn't do anything wrong.

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:43.318
Are you already better?

00:15:43.318 --> 00:15:45.779
They said I can leave the hospital.

00:15:45.779 --> 00:15:48.365
But, you had surgery...

00:15:48.365 --> 00:15:49.366
Yeah.

00:15:52.535 --> 00:15:56.998
I guess that's... because you're you?

00:15:58.249 --> 00:16:02.087
You're going somewhere again, aren't you?

00:16:02.087 --> 00:16:05.507
This is the train that heads out of town.

00:16:05.507 --> 00:16:09.135
Are you going off to fight alone again?

00:16:30.782 --> 00:16:32.617
Thank you.

00:16:33.702 --> 00:16:36.913
You've protected me so many times.

00:16:36.913 --> 00:16:41.418
But I guess going forward, you'll never...

00:16:42.669 --> 00:16:44.295
you...

00:16:46.506 --> 00:16:50.927
you won't let me protect <i>you</i>, will you?

00:16:59.894 --> 00:17:03.481
You still can't find their sniping point?!

00:17:03.481 --> 00:17:05.316
I am searching.

00:17:16.369 --> 00:17:20.457
You've gotten stronger. Thanks to <i>him</i>, eh?

00:17:20.457 --> 00:17:23.168
It's not in my nature to
completely rely on someone.

00:17:23.168 --> 00:17:28.006
I see. It would seem his ideas
are panning out well, for the moment.

00:17:28.006 --> 00:17:31.968
But having one person
as decoy is somewhat reckless.

00:17:31.968 --> 00:17:35.096
Save your thoughts on whether it's
reckless for once this is over!

00:17:35.096 --> 00:17:38.183
Very well. I'll battle you as much as you like!

00:17:38.183 --> 00:17:39.809
Restoration!

00:17:57.702 --> 00:17:58.703
It's delicious...

00:18:04.709 --> 00:18:09.297
<i>He's so fast. </i>
<i>And he can read all my movements.</i>

00:18:18.598 --> 00:18:21.768
The competition is over!
The 1st Platoon has shown the 17th

00:18:21.768 --> 00:18:24.771
just what a difference in power there is!

00:18:24.771 --> 00:18:26.856
Wh-What?!

00:18:26.856 --> 00:18:30.860
That wasn't a battle at all. You lose, Nina.

00:18:41.329 --> 00:18:43.748
So you were kind enough to come.

00:18:43.748 --> 00:18:46.501
I'd like to ask for some specifics, if I may.

00:18:46.501 --> 00:18:48.837
The truth is, there's
something wrong with the city.

00:18:48.837 --> 00:18:50.422
The city?

00:18:50.422 --> 00:18:53.216
Zuellni has suddenly begun to run amok.

00:18:53.216 --> 00:18:57.012
The contaminoids that I want
you to defeat lie in the city's path.

00:18:57.012 --> 00:19:01.099
Zuellni itself has changed
course toward the contaminoids.

00:19:01.099 --> 00:19:03.810
Itself?! But why?

00:19:03.810 --> 00:19:06.730
That, of course, is because of the Fallen One.

00:19:06.730 --> 00:19:08.606
Haia! You're still here?!

00:19:08.606 --> 00:19:12.610
Hey, don't go makin' that scary face now.

00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:15.697
I would like you to perform
this next task working with them.

00:19:15.697 --> 00:19:19.617
After all, they were the ones
who presented me with this information.

00:19:19.617 --> 00:19:20.827
Huh? But...

00:19:20.827 --> 00:19:25.331
Our probe has already confirmed
that contaminoids are in our travel path.

00:19:25.331 --> 00:19:28.376
And then there was
what befell you the other day.

00:19:28.376 --> 00:19:32.589
What if that were not simply
a case of deterioration?

00:19:38.053 --> 00:19:40.597
Put simply, the Fallen Ones
are city spirits run amok,

00:19:40.597 --> 00:19:42.724
and they bring ruin.

00:19:42.724 --> 00:19:46.353
Similar incidents are occurring
throughout the city.

00:19:46.353 --> 00:19:50.815
The Fallen Ones are tryin' to
bring destruction to Zuellni, too.

00:19:50.815 --> 00:19:51.941
No!

00:19:51.941 --> 00:19:56.237
If this is true, we will
need these men to remain here.

00:19:56.237 --> 00:20:01.076
Both to capture the Fallen Ones
and to aid us against the contaminoids.

00:20:01.076 --> 00:20:05.914
Oh, yeah. It's perfect timing,
so let me introduce ya.

00:20:05.914 --> 00:20:10.377
This is Fellmouse,
the nen'i operator who supports us.

00:20:10.377 --> 00:20:14.255
His vocal chords are no good,
so he can only talk with a vocalizer.

00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:19.052
It's an honor, Layfon Alseif-<i>dono</i>.

00:20:19.052 --> 00:20:21.930
This guy's a genius at nen'i.

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:24.182
What's more, he's got a special ability:

00:20:24.182 --> 00:20:26.851
He knows the contaminoids' smell.

00:20:26.851 --> 00:20:27.936
Smell?

00:20:27.936 --> 00:20:31.815
I have a particular sense of smell
when it comes to contaminoids.

00:20:31.815 --> 00:20:34.359
However, to properly
capture the contaminoids' scent,

00:20:34.359 --> 00:20:37.487
I must be physically outside,
beyond the air filters.

00:20:37.487 --> 00:20:41.282
Hence my body's current condition.

00:20:41.282 --> 00:20:45.161
But even that hasn't
been enough to kill this dude.

00:20:45.161 --> 00:20:46.996
I don't know whether it's genetic abnormality

00:20:46.996 --> 00:20:51.793
or that I've succeeded in acquiring
some special metabolic faculty...

00:20:51.793 --> 00:20:55.005
If my body were examined,
perhaps the day would come

00:20:55.005 --> 00:20:59.467
that people may
transcend contaminated substances.

00:20:59.467 --> 00:21:03.722
Please place your trust in my senses...

00:21:03.722 --> 00:21:06.808
You who have been recognized by our queen.

00:21:06.808 --> 00:21:10.186
You will go, won't you?

00:21:10.186 --> 00:21:14.733
Very well. But... I have one thing to ask.

00:21:17.986 --> 00:21:20.196
Never have I lost so disgracefully!

00:21:20.196 --> 00:21:23.158
This makes my having joined
the platoon meaningless!

00:21:23.158 --> 00:21:25.285
Cut that out, Siena.

00:21:25.285 --> 00:21:26.745
Don't address me like that!

00:21:26.745 --> 00:21:28.747
Just calm down.

00:21:28.747 --> 00:21:31.875
<i>I was overly confident in my abilities.</i>

00:21:31.875 --> 00:21:35.712
<i>I didn't dream I'd relied</i>
<i>on Layfon to this extent...</i>

00:21:38.298 --> 00:21:39.841
You...

00:21:39.841 --> 00:21:43.053
What is it? Has something happened
with my brother?

00:21:43.053 --> 00:21:46.222
I have been entrusted with
a message from Layfon Alseif

00:21:46.222 --> 00:21:48.308
to Nina Antalk.

00:21:48.308 --> 00:21:50.143
From Layfon?

00:22:01.446 --> 00:22:04.824
I'd like you to get this to Layfon.

00:22:06.076 --> 00:22:12.582
I prepared this as proof of
having received all Saiharden techniques.

00:22:16.252 --> 00:22:18.880
I'm to give this... to Layfon?

00:22:18.880 --> 00:22:21.299
Will you go for me?

00:22:21.299 --> 00:22:22.967
Yes!

00:22:26.554 --> 00:22:36.648
<i>Haikei, anata wa dare o omotteimasu ka</i>

00:22:36.648 --> 00:22:43.738
<i>Kono tegami wa mada mune no naka</i>

00:22:43.738 --> 00:22:53.790
<i>Totsuzen fureta anata no kioku no kakera</i>

00:22:53.790 --> 00:23:00.880
<i>Kokoro ni sasatte, ugokenai</i>

00:23:00.880 --> 00:23:05.719
<i>Kizuite hoshii, kizukanaide</i>

00:23:05.719 --> 00:23:09.431
<i>Tsumetaku suru no wa koi no sei? </i>

00:23:09.431 --> 00:23:19.024
<i>Tsutaetai yo, soba ni ite yo, demo ienai</i>

00:23:19.816 --> 00:23:28.408
<i>Yogoreta kono sekai de anata ni deaeta yo</i>

00:23:28.408 --> 00:23:39.586
<i>Watashi no kokoro ni maiorita</i>
<i>kiseki kanadete kudasai</i>

00:23:39.586 --> 00:23:47.427
<i>Ai no Zuellni</i>

00:23:53.975 --> 00:23:56.770
<i>Together with the</i>
<i>Salinban Mercenary Training Group,</i>

00:23:56.770 --> 00:23:59.147
<i>Layfon heads out to engage</i>
<i>a group of twelve contaminoids.</i>

00:23:59.147 --> 00:24:01.483
<i>And to investigate why Zuellni is running amok,</i>

00:24:01.483 --> 00:24:04.027
<i>Nina will go alone to the machinery department.</i>

00:24:04.027 --> 00:24:06.821
<i>Next time, "Salinban Mercenary Training Group,</i>
<i>Move Out!" and...</i>

00:24:06.821 --> 00:24:08.128
<i>Restoration!</i>
